  "id": "identity-diffusion",
  "term": "identity diffusion",
  "definition": "Identity diffusion is a disturbance in identity development marked by a poorly integrated sense of oneself and of other people, with weak boundaries between self and others. It is linked to difficulties in personality functioning such as intimacy, empathy, and self-direction, and is considered an important feature in borderline personality disorder.",
